+#
+#    Bots.UpdateInterval
+#        Description: (GuildAdventure: CP-11) A character without a client (a bot: its session has
+#                     no open socket) is updated (Player::Update: auras, position, regeneration, its
+#                     AI) once every this many milliseconds, each bot at a phase of its own, so the
+#                     bots of a map are spread over the world ticks; the time in between is handed to
+#                     its next update. Its session's packets are handled every tick. A character a
+#                     client plays is updated every tick.
+#        Default:     75
+#                     0 - (every character every world tick)
+
+Bots.UpdateInterval = 75
+
+#
+#    Bots.GridActivationRange
+#        Description: (GuildAdventure: CP-12) The range (yards) around a character without a client
+#                     (a bot) in which the cells of a continent are kept awake (creatures, game
+#                     objects updated). What a client sees is woken by the client's own character.
+#                     Dungeons and battlegrounds keep the map's visibility range. Off by default:
+#                     at 1600 bots 60 yards made the world tick slower, not faster (load test of
+#                     2026-11-21, mod-guild-adventure docs/performance.md section 10).
+#        Default:     0 - (the map's visibility range, as for a client)
+#                     60 - (the range the performance plan proposed)
+
+Bots.GridActivationRange = 0
+
 #
 #    MoveMaps.Enable
 #        Description: Enable/Disable pathfinding using mmaps - recommended.
